
# Dialog: ONE component for the author, the platform's own presentation underneath (native-dom-0026). The build fills
# `{platform}` from its env chain: macOS, iOS and Android reach ./native/toolkit/dialog.tree (an NSPanel sheet on the
# window, a page sheet, an android.app.Dialog) through their `toolkit` rung, and every other target, the web among
# them, falls to the generic ./native/dialog.tree. Both take `host`, `class`, `control` (open or closed, a disclosure
# from logic/disclosure), `title`, and `content`, the task that draws what the dialog holds. For a modal drawn by the
# theme rather than the platform, use `modal`. See note/term/app/11-uniform-interface.md.
#
#   save asking, call make-disclosure / bind start, false
#   call dialog / read root / text <> / read asking / text <Delete the file?> / read confirm-buttons

bear @term/face/code/component/native/{platform}/dialog
